From 7e431fc82b225aa15bc468e78b9990a6177332fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 08:46:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/38] WIP: W=1..8 logits width-purity probe (the last
 promotion gate)

tests/test-logits-width-probe.cpp: feed an identical prefix as one prefill batch,
then decode a W-token batch; row j sees the same context for every W, so its
logits must not depend on W.  Runs W=1..8 in separate contexts, checks every row
shared with the W=8 batch bit for bit, and prints per-row logits hashes so two
builds can be diffed.  Env RS=n_rs_seq, FA, KV.

Gate PASSES:
  P=256  (below MMB_MIN_T=512, MMB unreachable)  MMB on == off, bit-identical
  P=1024 MMB on != off (approved prefill re-baseline)  width_purity PASS maxdiff 0
  P=2048 MMB on != off (approved prefill re-baseline)  width_purity PASS maxdiff 0

Read in two halves: below the threshold MMB never runs in either the prefill or
the decode batch, so the two configs are bit-identical across every row of every
width - that is the 'identical by construction' claim demonstrated.  Above it the
hashes differ because MMB replaces the MMQ reduction with a dequant-to-bf16 WMMA
one (the approved re-baseline), while width_purity stays PASS with MMB on - MMB
introduces no width dependence, and the T >= 512 gate is what keeps it out of the
W <= 8 band.

Two probe bugs, same class as the -md trap: llama_batch_init(ubatch) sizes for the
micro-batch so a P-token prefill overruns it (silent SIGSEGV, plus a GGML_ASSERT
abort for the n_batch half); and n_batch (per llama_decode) vs n_ubatch (per
micro-batch) are different knobs, both must scale with P.  Also fixed: the first
per-W 'hash=' hashed the std::vector objects rather than the floats.
---
